From cb46d6c82f7e29b901b871d8c8a229998dcaeff4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:54:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] diag(dsv41): record non-finite MoE gate rows instead of
 asserting (#842 census)

Base: candidate-37 (vLLM patch head 5b7cfa37f). Diagnostic only, never for
serving: for the #842 crash repro (route_partials: gate logits contain nan or
inf, under copy drafts).

TileLangGateRouter flags a routed decode row whose gate partials do not sum to
finite logits (rows route_partials' mask skips are not looked at), records it
in a per-router buffer and zeroes its partials, so route_partials' assert does
not fire and the step finishes: the row routes to weight-0 experts and its
hidden state stays non-finite. Device-only torch ops, captured with the decode
graphs.

The V2 runner reads the census after the step's sampling (the target's rows)
and after the drafter proposes (the drafter's), a host sync each, and logs at
ERROR, as NONFINITE lines: the step's requests (rows, sampled, the copy
proposal being verified, total length) and every flagged row's layer, row,
request, slot, draft index, position, input id, padding flag, origin (anchor,
copy, dspark, placeholder) and whether it lies past the first rejected draft.

Tests: tests/kernels/moe/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_router.py (a NaN and an
inf row recorded, padding not looked at, other rows as before, cleared on
read, under CUDA-graph replay).

Upstream: not for upstream; a lab image's patch.
